  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 09c5317b33ca1a348b364d39cdb12d89, type: 3}
  m_Name: Old Manager Dialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  speakerName: Old Manager
  sentences:
  - Ahem... hello! You made it.
  - Let me show you the ropes of pizza-making!
  - First things first. This is the counter, were you will take the customers orders.
  - Customers will come up to the counter to order their pizzas. Press 'E' to interact
    with them and take their order.
  - Look at the icon by the customers head to see what kind of pizza they ordered.
  - You will also automatically take their order down on your orders notepad.
  - To start, Pick up a pizza base and place it in the preparation area. Then, place
    the ingredients the customer ordered on top of the pizza base.
  - Once you've done that, you can pick up the prepared pizza and place it inside
    the oven.
  - Once your pizza is done cooking, you can take it out the oven. Be careful not
    to burn it!
  - Then, place the completed pizza on the counter for the customer to pick it up.
  - If you ever forget how to make pizzas, just look at the tutorial poster on the
    wall for a reminder!
  - This is the restaurant computer where you can purchase upgrades and items.
  - The 'RatAway' website has all the rat repellents you need!
  - Err... the rats. Right. That brings me to my next point..
  - You'll notice that as you run your restaurant, rats will sometimes appear.
  - In order to dispose of them, you should use tools you can purchase from the 'RatAway'
    website.
  - If too many rats infest the restaurant and create dirt, customers will start
    noticing, and your restaurant rating will go down.
  - Your restaurants reputation is ranked with stars. Currently it's at 0 stars,
    but I believe you can achieve a 5 star restaurant some day!
  - Make sure to serve customers the correct order quickly, and keep the restaurant
    clean and maintained. You'll get there in no time!
  - Every now and then, the inspector will come to your restaurant to check its cleanliness.
    If you haven't been taking care of the rats, he will notice!
  - 
